@startuml rag-retriever
' The retriever query pipeline as a sequence: text → embedding → backend top-k →
' metadata join → threshold/synopsis filter → ranked results. Colour:
'   #2E7D32 green = embeddings   #6A1B9A purple = retrieval   #00838F teal = storage
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/rag-retriever.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/components/rag/retriever.md §3.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ParticipantFontColor white
skinparam ParticipantFontStyle bold
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
skinparam sequence {
  LifeLineBorderColor #90A4AE
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #ECEFF1
}
title Retriever<B>::query — one text query, end to end

actor "Caller" as user #455A64
participant "Retriever<B>" as r #6A1B9A
participant "ModernBertEmbedder" as e #2E7D32
participant "RagIndex<B>" as idx #00838F
participant "B: RetrievalBackend" as b #6A1B9A

user -> r : **query(“what is dense retrieval?”)**\n&mut self — the embedder caches
activate r

r -> e : embed_query(q)
activate e
note right of e
  Tokenise (≤ 8 192 tokens) → ModernBERT
  → pool (CLS) → normalise.
  A **query** and a **document** are embedded by
  the //same// encoder into the //same// ℝ⁷⁶⁸ —
  that shared space is what makes ⟨v̂_q , v̂_d⟩
  meaningful.
end note
e --> r : v_q ∈ ℝ⁷⁶⁸
deactivate e

r -> idx : query(v_q, config.top_k)
activate idx

idx -> b : query(v_q, top_k)
activate b
note right of b
  Exact: one ""sgemv"" over the n × d matrix,
  then introselect for the k largest.
  HNSW: greedy descent, beam ef_search.
end note
b --> idx : Vec<(DocumentId, f32)>\nsorted by score ↓
deactivate b

idx -> idx : **filter_map** id ↦ documents[id]\n(ids with no metadata are dropped)
idx --> r : Vec<(DocumentMeta, f32)>
deactivate idx

r -> r : **filter**\n① score ≥ min_similarity\n② include_explicit_synopsis\n③ include_generated_synopsis
r -> r : **rank** — enumerate() ⇒ rank = i + 1

r --> user : Vec<RetrievalResult>\nuri · title · synopsis · score · rank
deactivate r

note over r, b
  **Ranks are assigned before filtering is applied.**
  ""enumerate()"" runs on the raw top-k, so a result
  surviving a ""min_similarity"" cut keeps the index it
  had among the //unfiltered// hits: ranks stay faithful
  to the backend's ordering but may contain gaps.
end note
@enduml
